<BaseLayout title="Police Drones / UAS | Surveillance | NoRec.US" description="Illinois law-enforcement drone use, statutory safeguards, reporting, and documented local deployments." active="surveillance">
<main class="page_shell">
<header class="article_header">
<p class="eyebrow">SURVEILLANCE TECHNOLOGY · AERIAL</p>
<h1>Police drones / unmanned aircraft systems</h1>
<p class="article_deck">Illinois regulates law-enforcement drone use through the Freedom from Drone Surveillance Act, including permitted uses, disclosure rules, and public reporting requirements.</p>
</header>

<section class="evidence_box"><span class="status_label">DOCUMENTED IN ILLINOIS</span><p>The Freedom from Drone Surveillance Act governs law-enforcement drone use. It includes warrant-based and emergency exceptions and provides that records such as flight-path data, metadata, or telemetry of specific flights may be disclosed subject to FOIA.</p></section>

<section>
<p class="eyebrow">DOCUMENTED LOCAL EXAMPLES</p><h2>Agency inventories and reported flights</h2>
<div class="finding_grid">
<article><span class="status_label">DOCUMENTED</span><h3>Huntley Police</h3><p>The statewide SFY 2024 reporting material records two Huntley Police drones and 38 flights during the reporting period.</p></article>
<article><span class="status_label">DOCUMENTED</span><h3>McHenry County Sheriff</h3><p>The same reporting dataset records two Sheriff's Office drones and 24 flights during the reporting period.</p></article>
<article><span class="status_label">DOCUMENTED</span><h3>Winnebago County Sheriff</h3><p>The SFY 2024 report lists nine drones and 13 flights, including search, event-overwatch, damage-assessment, and crash-reconstruction uses.</p></article>
<article><span class="status_label">DOCUMENTED</span><h3>DeKalb County Sheriff</h3><p>The report lists three drones and seven flights. The Sheriff's Office also publishes a UAS policy covering retention, prohibited uses, disclosure, and facial-recognition restrictions.</p></article>
<article><span class="status_label">DOCUMENTED</span><h3>DeKalb Police</h3><p>The statewide report lists one DeKalb Police drone; the department publishes a current UAS policy.</p></article>
<article><span class="status_label">DOCUMENTED</span><h3>South Elgin Police</h3><p>The statewide report lists two drones and 43 flights during the reporting period.</p></article>
</div>
</section>

<section>
<p class="eyebrow">EVIDENCE SCOPE</p><h2>What a deployment record can establish.</h2>
<p>Drone inventories and flight counts describe only part of a program. Policies, flight logs, statutory purpose categories, payloads and sensors, video retention, evidence exports, mutual-aid use, training, and vendor systems establish additional operational context. NoRec attributes each claim to the source that supports it.</p>
</section>

